.TH REGRET 1 "2026-09-30" "Bad Decisions Client 2.2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
regret \- deal rounds from a Bad Decisions API
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B regret
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B regret deal
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B regret health
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B regret feedback
.RI {enjoy|regret|clear} " [" options ]
.br
.B regret provenance
.RI [ --json ]
.br
.B regret identity
.RI {status|reset|off|on}
.br
.B regret consequences
.RI {status|enjoy|regret|enable|disable}
.br
.B regret together
.RI room " [--name display-name] [--api-url url] [--timeout seconds] [--heartbeat seconds] [--tui]"
.br
.B regret doctor
.RI [ --api-url " url]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B regret
is the dependency-light terminal client for a Bad Decisions service. It deals rounds, lists packs, checks health, records optional feedback, and prints provenance from the last local draw.
.PP
Consequences is opt-in. It controls both voting and the pseudonymous telemetry required for voting. Non-interactive use leaves it disabled unless an explicit preference is already stored.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --version
Print the installed version and exit.
.TP
.BI "--api-url " url
Use a compatible API endpoint. The default is https://bytes.coffee/bad-decisions.
.TP
.BI "--packs " ids
Comma-separated pack IDs for both colors.
.TP
.BI "--prompt-packs " ids
Override the prompt-pack selector.
.TP
.BI "--answer-packs " ids
Override the answer-pack selector.
.TP
.BR --list-packs
List packs from the service.
.TP
.BR --health
Check service health.
.TP
.BR --json
Print machine-readable JSON where supported.
.TP
.BI "--timeout " seconds
Network timeout. Must be greater than zero.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B deal
Deal and print one round. This is the default command.
.TP
.B health
Check the API health endpoint.
.TP
\fBfeedback\fR \fBenjoy\fR|\fBregret\fR|\fBclear\fR
Submit, change, or withdraw the last eligible vote. Requires Enjoy Consequences.
.TP
\fBprovenance\fR [\fB--json\fR]
Print license, attribution, version, and source metadata for packs in the last saved draw without contacting the API.
.TP
\fBidentity\fR \fBstatus\fR|\fBreset\fR|\fBoff\fR|\fBon\fR
Inspect, rotate, omit, or restore the local pseudonymous installation identity. Identity use is still subordinate to Consequences consent.
.TP
.B consequences status
Show whether Consequences is enabled.
.TP
.B consequences enjoy
Enable voting and stable-ID pseudonymous vote telemetry.
.TP
.B consequences regret
Disable voting and vote telemetry entirely.
.TP
.BR "consequences enable" ", " "consequences disable"
Aliases for enjoy and regret.
.TP
.BI "together " room
Join or reconnect to an ephemeral Peer Pressure multiplayer room. The first participant is the initial Responsible Adult. The client maintains authenticated heartbeats, submits private answers, and resynchronizes stale room state automatically. Use --name when no saved room session exists. --heartbeat sets the heartbeat interval in seconds (default 5).
.PP
Add
.B --tui
to use the optional full-screen Textual table. It displays players, scores, presence, the Responsible Adult, prompt, private hand, anonymous judging choices, and result together. Install it with
.BR "pipx install 'bad-decisions-client[tui]'" .
The line-oriented interface remains the dependency-free default. In the TUI, q closes the table even when the service cannot be told you left, and the room's host presses e twice (or End room) to end the room for everyone.
.PP
The official hosted service also provides an install-free browser table at https://bytes.coffee/bad-decisions/peerpressure. It uses the same rooms and protocol as Regret.
.PP
The prompt follows the room: the room's host presses s to start (and becomes the first Responsible Adult), players choose answers by number (comma-separated when a prompt needs several), the Responsible Adult picks the consequence, and Enter refreshes or advances. q leaves the room. The room's host may type e at any prompt, then y to confirm, to end the room for everyone; leaving never ends a room, and an abandoned room expires six hours (by default) after its last change. When the service refuses an action, regret prints its reason and message, with a hint when the display name is taken or the game has already started.
.TP
.BI doctor " [--api-url url]"
Check this installation and print a fix for each problem, changing nothing: how regret was installed, whether it is on PATH, whether
.B man regret
finds this page (behind pyenv or asdf shims it cannot, and doctor prints the MANPATH line to add), preference file permissions, and whether the service answers. Exits 1 if a check fails.
.SH INSTALLATION
Homebrew is the suggested install on macOS and Linux and includes the Peer Pressure TUI:
.B brew install bytesandcoffee/tap/regret
also links this page into Homebrew's manual path. pipx install bad-decisions-client and pip install bad-decisions-client also work; installers cannot run setup code, so use regret doctor to check shell integration.
.PP
Python package installers provide the TUI through the optional \fBbad-decisions-client[tui]\fR extra; the base Python package remains dependency-free.
.SH CONSENT
On the first interactive deal, an unset or stale consent preference prompts once. Choose Enjoy Consequences or Regret Consequences. The choice and consent schema version are stored locally and survive upgrades. Pressing Enter chooses regret. Non-interactive invocations never block for consent.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.regret.env
Atomic local preferences and pseudonymous identity state.
.TP
.I ~/.regret-last-round.json
The last draw's provenance and, when eligible, its feedback capability.
.TP
.I ~/.regret-peer-pressure.json
Protected room-local player IDs and reconnect capabilities. Written atomically with mode 0600. These identities are independent of Consequences.
.SH PRIVACY
No account is required. A stable pseudonymous identifier is used only when Consequences is enabled. Disabling Consequences disables voting and its telemetry. The client does not use this identifier for update checks or Peer Pressure; version checks are cached and use the configured API health endpoint. Peer Pressure sends only the authenticated room-local identity and state needed for gameplay.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Network, configuration, or unavailable-feedback failure.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line usage.
